<section style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="label red" style="margin:0 0 20px">How we fix it</p>
  <h2 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(36px,4.5vw,58px);margin:0 0 56px;max-width:820px">Three steps, in this order.</h2>
  <div class="g3"><div class="card reveal" style="min-height:240px"><p class="label" style="margin:0 0 14px">Step 01</p><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:28px;margin:0 0 12px">Review the priority pages</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:15px">We start with the collections and products that sell the most, or should sell more.</p></div><div class="card reveal" style="min-height:240px"><p class="label" style="margin:0 0 14px">Step 02</p><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:28px;margin:0 0 12px">Rewrite for the buyer, then tune</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:15px">Titles, headings and copy are written around what the shopper needs to know. Search fit comes second, not first.</p></div><div class="card reveal" style="min-height:240px"><p class="label" style="margin:0 0 14px">Step 03</p><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:28px;margin:0 0 12px">Link guides and products together</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:15px">Guides link to the products they recommend. Products link back to the guides that help people choose.</p></div></div>
</div></section>
<section style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="narrow">
  <div style="background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:26px;padding:50px">
